WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.460
Get online, save data, and spot a fake website.

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:10.490
This is the video for module one of Internet Basics and Online Safety: getting online with your smartphone.

3
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:18.700
The internet is a huge network of cables, masts and servers. Think of it as the roads that join towns.

4
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:25.470
The World Wide Web is the pages you open in a browser, like the shops along those roads.

5
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.890
Your phone gets online with mobile data, which uses your bundle, or Wi-Fi from a nearby router.

6
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:41.520
The letters by your signal bars matter. E or 2G is very slow. 4G or LTE is good for video.

7
00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:52.770
Here is an example from the course. Halima in Kaduna has a video call with her cooperative. Ten minutes before, her screen shows one bar and the letter E.

8
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.880
She knows E means very slow 2G, too slow for video.

9
00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:04.080
So she walks about 20 metres to the front of the compound. Now she sees three bars and 4G.

10
00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:11.390
She turns off a weak Wi-Fi that keeps dropping, joins the call, and switches her own camera off to keep it steady.

11
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:17.370
Tip: if pages will not load, turn Airplane mode on for ten seconds, then off again.

12
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.970
Now, data. Open Settings, search for Data Saver and turn it on.

13
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:31.790
In WhatsApp, go to Storage and data, then Media auto-download. On mobile data, choose photos only or nothing.

14
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.260
In the same menu, turn on Use less data for calls.

15
00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:44.080
When watching videos, tap the gear icon, then Quality, and choose Data saver or 360p.

16
00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:53.890
In Play Store, set updates to Over Wi-Fi only. And remember: video uses the most data, and higher quality uses much more.

17
00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:02.690
For example, Ifeoma in Onitsha buys a 30-day bundle of about 6GB, but it keeps finishing in two weeks.

18
00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:13.560
She opens Mobile data usage in Settings. Facebook used about 2.5GB. She sets its videos to autoplay only on Wi-Fi.

19
00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:21.770
Play Store updates used about 1GB, so she sets updates to Wi-Fi only, and turns on Data Saver.

20
00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:28.090
The next month her bundle lasts the full 30 days, with about 1GB left over.

21
00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:37.040
Buy bundles only through your network official code or app, or your bank app. Never pay a stranger promising cheap 50GB.

22
00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:48.060
In the browser address bar you can type a web address or your search words. Type the important words, not a long sentence, and add your town when it matters.

23
00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.200
Put quotation marks around an exact phrase to keep it together.

24
00:02:54.450 --> 00:03:03.830
Type site, a colon, then an official address, to search only that site. Nigerian government sites usually end in dot gov dot n g.

25
00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:16.540
Results marked Sponsored are paid adverts, and scammers sometimes copy real brands. Bisi in Abeokuta nearly paid a fake 3,500 naira fee this way.

26
00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:26.640
Grace in Port Harcourt got an SMS telling her to update her BVN at a link. She did not tap it. She pressed and held it to read the address.

27
00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:36.210
The rule is: read the domain just before the first single slash. Scammers put a famous name at the front so it looks right at a glance.

28
00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:47.510
Her link ended in gtbank-ng-update dot com. That is not her bank's real domain. Watch for look-alike spelling, wrong endings and shortened links.

29
00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:55.800
She opened her bank's official app, saw no warning, and called the number on the back of her ATM card to report it.

30
00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:06.070
A common mistake is trusting HTTPS. Scam sites can have it too. It means the line is private, not that the site is honest.

31
00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:15.520
If a shopping or job site shows two or more of these signs, stop. Search its name with the word scam, and ask someone you trust.

32
00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:25.000
To remember. The internet is the network, and the Web is the pages. Video eats the most data, so turn on Data Saver.

33
00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:35.080
Buy bundles only through official channels. Read the domain before the first single slash. And for money, type the address or use the official app.

34
00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:45.270
Now practise. Map your signal, put your phone on a data diet, try the search challenge, and find the real domains of three sites you use.

35
00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.560
Continue with the lessons below.
